i3status-rust for Debian
------------------------

This package ships no configuration file. i3status-rs has no defaults to fall
back on -- it needs a config to know which blocks to render -- but the config
is per-user, so there is nothing in /etc for dpkg to track and nothing to merge
on upgrade.

To get started, copy the shipped example and edit your copy:

  /usr/share/doc/i3status-rust/examples/config.toml

to ~/.config/i3status-rust/config.toml, then point i3 at it:

  bar {
      status_command i3status-rs ~/.config/i3status-rust/config.toml
  }

The icon and theme sets are installed to /usr/share/i3status-rust and are
selected by name in the config's [icons] and [theme] tables. A set of the same
name under ~/.config/i3status-rust or ~/.local/share/i3status-rust takes
precedence, so a custom theme does not have to replace the packaged one.

Most icon sets use glyphs from a Nerd Font or Font Awesome. The Recommends on
fonts-font-awesome covers the "awesome*" sets; the "material-nf" set needs a
patched Nerd Font, which Debian does not package.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
